led  within him let's just say for the most  of the series Naruto's relationship with  Kurama has been rocky to say the least  the moment the two decide to put their  differences aside in the fourth shinobi  world war and work together is a moment  that would send chills down any fan  spine it's a necessary step forward in  the hero's journey and the scene of the  Shonan hero finally coming to terms with  the powers that he's shunned for so long  is truly a sight to behold it looks  great when it happened in Bleach and it  certainly looks awesome as hell in this  series  [Music]  like everything's okay  [Music]  Cochran or little convener  what you do is huge here bring goods the  next entry on the list is the third  hokages sacrifice during invasion of  Konoha Naruto's a series full of  heartache and death and one of the very  first instances of this is when the  Third Hokage  sarutobi dies in the climax of the Kanoa  crush arc in an effort to stop the  deceptive and powerful Orochimaru  sarutobi invokes the Shinigami realizing  that he still has no power to defeat the  evil shinobi for good  sarutobi decides on the next best course  of action sealing the evil shinobi  through the arms and preventing him from  using ninjutsu at the cost of invoking  the Shinigami however sarutobi has to  pay with his very own life so Tobias  death marks one of the first major  losses that Naruto fans had to  experience orochimaru's invasion has  been repelled by the cost of the  villages biggest cornerstone  [Music]  host up next we have the reveal of  Toby's true identity ever since his  introduction the Toby character has been  an enigma constantly shifting from  comedy relief to credible threat on a  whim a few would have expected the mask  Toby to be one of the last Akatsuki  members left standing turns out that  Toby's actually obito uchiha who  proceeds to further add fuel to the fire  of the fourth shinobi world war his  subsequent battles with the heroes  culminating with him taking control of  the ten tails are some of my favourite  fights in the final arc it also helps  that he gets some redemption towards the  end making a nice personal parallel to  Naruto  [Music]  [Applause]  next up we have guy opening the eight  gate to take on mother er but most of  the series fans have seen Mike guy as  the epitome of that one strong yet  quirky character while we know of him as  a master of the eight gates technique  guy mostly spent most of the series as a  goofy mentor figure for our heroes it  would take until the latter parts of the  story before we witness what he's really  capable of forget him being capable of  defeating kisame which is a feat that's  impressive in its own right Martha one  of the most powerful ninjas in the world  is made to respect guys strength after  receiving a dose of the full power of  the eight gates this is the first time  we ever see all eight gates being  released in battle and boy is it a  spectacle while it didn't do the trick  in ending mother earth not that anything  worked anyway seeing the pinnacle of the  techniques a sight to behold  [Applause]  next on the list is Itachi's battle  against Sasuke and the revelation of the  truth behind the Uchiha clan Massacre  one of the main driving forces behind  Sasuke's action in much of the series  revolved around getting stronger  for what purpose revenge against his  brother Itachi who murdered the entire  Uchiha clan leaving him as the only  survivor it would only be proper for the  brothers to have their fated showdown  and they delivered unleashing their  amazing techniques on one another it's  Sasuke who eventually came out on top  as if the emotional farewell between the  brothers isn't enough it's revealed that  Itachi had massacred the Uchiha clan in  order to prevent a coop deer tap which  would have led to a civil war the reveal  that Itachi had been a hero all along  was one twist that shook the very  foundations of the series  next we have moderate appearance in the  fourth shinobi war what an entrance  one deserved by no less than what many  consider to be the series real final  boss after being restored thanks to the  arrow tense a mother er lives up to all  the hype as he crashes into the  battlefield devastating the fourth  division in his wake we can see in that  very scene how far ahead he is and how  he effortlessly defeats an entire army  with his intelligence and prowess not  only that he proceeds to single-handedly  defeat the car gaze the tailed beasts  and pretty much everything thrown at him  miracle after miracle wouldn't be enough  to stop him from casting the infinite  tsukuyomi that engulfs the world it  would require some good old plot  convenience to finally put him down for  good yes kono mo know what I see what I  see this episode honest he'll say no  kousaka's no densetsu Nina's right there  merica number twos certainly one of the  most iconic losses for fans of the  series Jiraiya's death for the longest  time the pervy and ever lovable member  of the legendary sannin has been the  closest person to a father figure for  Naruto knowing this it kind of felt  inevitable that he would fall somewhere  down the line this just happens in his  mission to gather Intel he goes down in  a blaze of glory putting up one hell of  a fight against Conan and the numerous  panes before finally going down despite  lamenting over his failures as he faces  his end Jiraiya's death doesn't turn out  to be entirely gloom and doom make no  mistake this is one of the saddest  moments in the series however seeing  Jiraiya die with the smiles also one of  the most uplifting moments in the entire  series the Masters part in the story has  ended with his death but he knows for  world that he can leave the rest to his  young pupil to save the world  [Music]  call it it's Tom washing he not took on  all and finally the number one in the  list is the final battle between Naruto  and Sasuke  of course the series just had to end  this way it's as destined that the final  battle of the series would be a  no-holds-barred battle between the hero  and his rival Naruto and Sasuke are no  strangers to fighting each other but  this is the battle that culminates all  the build-up that's been set up since  early on in the series more than just a  battle of strength this is the ultimate  battle of philosophies that the series  take so much pride in if talk no Jitsu  is any indication  Sasuke can be seen as the culmination of  all the ideologies that Naruto had to  overcome in his journey and no one else  could be a more fitting final opponent  for our hero not murderer not Obito and  certainly not Kaguya the fact that the  final battle ended in a technical draw  with Naruto only winning over his  longtime rival through his ideology and  not his strength cements this as one of  the top moments in the series  Naruto's a series full of many more epic  touching and straight-up heartbreaking  moments I'm a hundred percent sure that  a top ten list wouldn't cover everything  in the series is decorated rum I hope to  hear from you in the comments section on  what moments you think should have been  included in the list and which is your  personal favorite leave a like if you  enjoyed this video and subscribe if you  haven't already for more anime content  I'll see you next time on vinnie tube  [Music]
 

